{"name":"Wallflower","hex":"#a0848a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wallflower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several short-lived herbs or shrubs of the Erysimum genus with bright yellow to red flowers.","Gastrolobium grandiflorum, a poisonous bushy shrub, endemic to Australia."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stand shyly apart from a dance, waiting to be asked to join in."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wallflower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wallflower (Diana Krall album)","blocks":[{"text":"Wallflower is the twelfth studio album by Canadian singer Diana Krall, released on February 3, 2015, by Verve Records. The album was produced by David Foster. The album's supporting tour, Wallflower World Tour, began in Boston on February 25, 2015."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/96/Diana_Krall_-_Wallflower.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wallflower_(Diana_Krall_album)"},{"title":"Wallflower (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Wallflower was an English rock band from South London. Formed in 2014 by Vinicius Moreira-Yeoell (vocals/guitar), Jake Reburn (guitar), Sam Woolley (guitar), Will Slane (bass) and Harley Clifton (drums), they released their debut EP Summer Daze later that year. On their second EP Where It Fell Apart, they began to incorporate elements of electronic and industrial music, such as synthesisers and sampling. By 2020, they were one of the forefront bands in British emo. Wallflower disbanded soon after the release of their debut album Teach Yourself to Swim (2020). They reunited in 2026."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wallflower_(band)"},{"title":"Erysimum","blocks":[{"text":"Erysimum, or wallflower, is a genus of flowering plants in the cabbage family, Brassicaceae. It includes more than 150 species, both popular garden plants and many wild forms. Erysimum is characterised by star-shaped trichomes growing from the stem, with yellow, red, pink or orange flowers and multiseeded seed pods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Erysimum-scoparium.jpg/330px-Erysimum-scoparium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erysimum"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg/120px-Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg/250px-Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg/120px-Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg/120px-ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg/250px-ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg/120px-ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Erysimum_helveticum.jpg/120px-Erysimum_helveticum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Erysimum_helveticum.jpg/250px-Erysimum_helveticum.jpg?utm_source=en.wi